comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T18:18:28.969Z","harness:codex","Implementation start: active in the cohesive automatic identity platform PR spanning the identity ADR, structured SDK provenance, precedence-safe observation, declarative harness registry, MCP/plugin configuration, and token-minimal help guidance. Duplicate check covered all 2,028 tracker items and live GitHub reports; no new item created."
  "2026-07-25T19:14:54.167Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: added declarative built-in and workspace/package harness signal registries with literal bounded environment, argv, process-label, and MCP client matching; model/session key precedence; normalized collision handling; identical-registration reference counting; settings validation, sparse persistence, CLI and MCP wiring; and SDK exports. Arbitrary commands, regex execution, filesystem probing, and network lookup are excluded. Packed isolated acceptance proved a workspace-defined harness end to end; full suite and 100% coverage passed."
  "2026-07-25T19:16:26.384Z","harness:codex","Acceptance finding and fix: a tracker evidence comment containing a harness name exposed that scanning every CLI argument could misclassify ordinary free text as a harness signal. Detection now bounds argv identity/model markers to the executable launch prefix (first three tokens); explicit process_labels remain the host-controlled extension seam. A regression test proves a later claude-code-agent comment value cannot spoof detection."
